<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Adaptive launcher icon — background layer (TASK-12, FR-41 / OQ-05).

    An alias for the brand light token in `res/values/colors.xml` (S11): the icon, the vector ink
    and the branding palette now have one definition each, so a brand tweak cannot leave the
    launcher on a stale hex value. The fill is the canon brand pairing's LIGHT token (#F6D32D,
    ui-design-bible §Colour & branding tokens, "Branding primary (light)"), not the in-editor
    palette: branding colours are identity/launch colours and are never used on editor chrome.

    CANON GAP: the canon names a DARK-mode adaptive-icon background variant (#873000, "Branding
    primary (dark)"). A per-scheme adaptive-icon background needs a `res/values-night/` colour
    override, which is outside this task's scope; safe to defer — the light token is the documented
    default, OQ-05 assigns final icon production (incl. dark variants) to the later Play wave, and
    the brand dark token is already the foreground ink so the mark keeps its identity on either
    background once the night variant lands.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">@color/brand_yellow</color>
</resources>
